[0m[0m
[38;5;10mprintf[0m is called through the C library's own [38;5;10mprintf[0m (extern variadic declaration) rather than Rust's [38;5;10mprintln![0m, so formatting and stdout buffering interleave identically with any other libc output in the host process. Verified byte-identical for file, pipe, and unbuffered stdout, and across edge values including [38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m/[38;5;10mINT_MAX[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mbad()[0m is the original defect (CWE-457/824: dereference of an uninitialized automatic pointer) and is preserved, not fixed. Getting it to behave like the C required matching [3mwhere[23m the uninitialized read lands. Idiomatic [38;5;10mMaybeUninit[0m + [38;5;10mread_volatile[0m reads a red-zone slot at [38;5;10mentry_rsp - 8[0m and segfaulted; the C compiler builds a frame and reads [38;5;10mentry_rsp - 16[0m, which holds stale mapped data. [38;5;10mbad[0m is therefore emitted as a naked function whose disassembly is instruction-for-instruction identical to the C [38;5;10m-O0[0m output (with a portable [38;5;10mMaybeUninit[0m fallback under [38;5;10mcfg(not(target_arch = "x86_64"))[0m). After this change, direct [38;5;10mbad()[0m calls print [38;5;10m0[0m and exit 0 in both libraries, stable over 20 runs plus ASLR-off and stack-padding perturbations.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
